The main goal of this strategy is to design products and packaging that can be easily reused. This includes using durable materials that can be easily disassembled and cleaned. It also involves designing products that can be easily refilled or reused in other ways. Typically, this approach is associated with circular business models, such as the "milkmen model" in which the customer pays a recurring fee for home delivery. A reusable packaging product would ideally be reused by numerous companies in order to be fully sustainable and circular. When packaging is reused, adjustments are made up and down the supply chain to ensure the fastest, most secure process possible for the consumer.